# Agent Tesla (2014 onwards). A keylogger and password stealer sold as a "monitoring tool", usually sent as a purchase-order attachment.
# A quest (QUESTS.md): the trainee works a purchasing shift, confirms one order safely, then meets Agent Tesla in the next "order". Agent Tesla went after buyers and shipping and logistics staff; the victim here is invented.
os windows
user Dana Okafor
about
  | Agent Tesla usually arrived as a "purchase order" email sent to buyers and shipping staff. The attachment was a program in a zip file, dressed up as a PDF. When run, it showed only a "damaged file" message, then recorded keys, copied text and screenshots, and mailed them to the attacker. This victim is invented, but the mail is the kind that hit purchasing teams for years.
story
  | You are Dana Okafor, purchasing assistant at Northwind Traders. Each day you confirm supplier orders in the company's supplier portal, and the suppliers you know are a short list.
  | It is mid-afternoon. You have confirmed 6 of today's 8 orders. Two to go.
  | Your portal sign-in and a few supplier details are in two text files on the desktop. That is a bad habit, but it keeps this training quick.
quota 6 8 Orders confirmed today

# Dana's desk: the details she copies from (soft flags: careless, but only here to keep the training simple).
file Desktop/portal-login.txt
  at 930 200
  | Northwind Supplier Portal
  | User ID: dana.okafor
  | Password: Orders-2026!
file Desktop/supplier-accounts.txt
  at 930 300
  | Supplier payment details (training copy)
  | Contoso Foods account: 55-0123-4567
  | Fabrikam Ltd account: 55-0456-7890

# The portal: a sign-in page, and the order pages behind it.
page portal-login supplier-portal.example/purchasing/sign-in
  title Supplier Portal: sign in
  brand Northwind Supplier Portal
  favorite
  heading Sign in to the Supplier Portal
  | Welcome back. Sign in to confirm your orders.
  field User ID = dana.okafor
  field secret Password = Orders-2026!
  button Sign in
page confirmed-2284 supplier-portal.example/purchasing/orders/done
  title Order confirmed
  brand Northwind Supplier Portal
  heading Order confirmed
  | PO-2284 to Contoso Foods: 40 cartons of dried goods, delivery on 12 November 2026.
page queried-2284 supplier-portal.example/purchasing/orders/queried
  title Order queried
  brand Northwind Supplier Portal
  heading Order sent back with a question
  | PO-2284 is on hold. Purchasing will check it with Contoso Foods.
page po-2284 supplier-portal.example/purchasing/orders/PO-2284
  title Confirm order: PO-2284
  brand Northwind Supplier Portal
  requires portal-login
  heading Confirm order: PO-2284
  | A supplier order is waiting for your confirmation.
  section Order
  row Supplier = Contoso Foods
  row Order = PO-2284, dated 2 November 2026
  row Goods = 40 cartons of dried goods
  row Delivery = 12 November 2026
  button Confirm order -> confirmed-2284
  button Query this order -> queried-2284

mail mail-2284
  from Priya Shah <priya.shah@northwind.example>
  subject Order PO-2284 to confirm (Contoso Foods)
  link po-2284
  | Hi Dana,
  |
  | Contoso's order for the dried goods is in the portal, ready for you to confirm. The link goes straight to it.
  |
  | Priya

step Order 7 of 8
  look Mail: Priya's message with the order link
  | A new order has come in from Priya, in Purchasing. This one is real. Confirm it the normal way, so you know what normal looks like.
notify mail Priya Shah
  | Order PO-2284 to confirm (Contoso Foods)

step The link goes to the portal
  look the link under Priya's message
  when mail mail-2284
  | The email links to the company's own portal, supplier-portal.example. Hover over a link before you click it, to check where it goes.
open mail-2284

step Sign in as usual
  look the two boxes: User ID and Password
  when visit po-2284
  move Copy the details from portal-login.txt on the desktop: click a box and press any keys to type, then click “Sign in”.
  | The portal asks you to sign in first. Two boxes: User ID and Password. Remember what this looks like.
open po-2284

step Check, then confirm
  look the supplier, the goods and the delivery date
  when choose portal-login 1
  | You are in. Check the supplier and the goods, then confirm the order or send it back with a question.
signin portal-login

step 7 of 8 done
  look the counter in the guide: one order left
  when choose po-2284 any
  | Done. One order to go. And another email has just arrived.
choose po-2284 1
quota +1

# The lure: a "PDF" in a zip that is a program.
view tesla-error message
  title Purchase order viewer
  icon error
  | PO-2291.pdf could not be opened. The file is damaged.
  button OK -> done primary
# The attacker's log: what this desk gave Agent Tesla, then examples of what it also takes (training copy).
view tesla-report panel
  title Attacker's log (training copy)
  app Agent Tesla report
  icon bug
  heading Report Agent Tesla tried to mail
  section Keys typed, grouped by window
  tone bad
  row Supplier Portal: sign in = dana.okafor, Orders-2026!
  note Every key press is written to the log, with the title of the window it went into.
  section Examples: not from this desk
  tone warn
  row Copied text = account numbers from a text file
  row Screenshots = one every few minutes
  row Saved logins = passwords stored in browsers and mail programs
  note Training copy. On this desk you did not copy text, take screenshots or read saved logins.
  button Close -> close primary

program tesla PO-2291.pdf
  publisher none
  signed no
  prompt open-warning
  description Purchase order viewer
  process RegAsm.exe
  cpu 6
  mem 54
  keylog yes
  parent PO-2291.pdf.exe
  command C:\Windows\Microsoft.NET\Framework\v4.0.30319\RegAsm.exe
  net smtp.harbour-trading.invalid:587
  startup PdfViewerUpdate C:\Users\Dana\AppData\Roaming\PdfViewerUpdate\updater.exe
  location HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Run
  view tesla-error
  selfdelete
folder Downloads/PO-2291.zip
file Downloads/PO-2291.zip/PO-2291.pdf.exe
  icon pdf
  program tesla
  size 612352
mail po
  from Purchasing <purchasing@harbour-trading.invalid>
  subject New order PO-2291, please confirm today
  attach Downloads/PO-2291.zip
  | Dear Dana,
  |
  | Please confirm the attached purchase order and the delivery date today. The zip is protected for security: the password is 2291.
  |
  | Purchasing Department
notify mail Purchasing
  | New order PO-2291, please confirm today

step An order from a stranger
  look the sender, and the zip file instead of a portal link
  when mail po
  cue file:fs-po-2291-pdf-exe-aca536a8 file:fs-po-2291-zip-23536816 app:files
  move Open the zip (the attachment, also in Downloads), then double-click the "PDF" inside.
  | A supplier Dana does not know, a zip file instead of the portal, and a password in the email. Real orders come through the portal. A password on a zip often only keeps mail filters from looking inside.
open po

step The warning before it runs
  look the security warning: an unknown publisher, or "a Windows program" on a Mac
  when prompt tesla
  | Inside the zip is a file that looks like PO-2291.pdf. Windows hides the end of its name (a Mac shows all of it): it is really PO-2291.pdf.exe, a program. Opening it makes the computer ask whether to run a program from an unknown publisher. A real PDF never asks this.
  | This is the last place the attack can be stopped. Many victims clicked Run.
open Downloads/PO-2291.zip/PO-2291.pdf.exe

step Only an error box
  look the "damaged file" message
  when run tesla
  move Press OK on the message, like Dana did.
  | The program shows a fake "damaged file" message, so Dana thinks the PDF is just broken and moves on. Behind it, Agent Tesla hides inside RegAsm.exe, a real Windows program, so the name looks safe.
answer run

step Find the process and start-up item
  look RegAsm.exe in the process list (Task Manager or Activity Monitor)
  when done tesla-error
  move Go back to work: open Mail and click Priya's last email.
  | Agent Tesla hides inside RegAsm.exe, a real program that nobody opened. It added itself as PdfViewerUpdate in the start-up list, so it starts again with the computer.
  | From now on it records every key you type. The process list and the start-up list show it, if you look.
open taskmanager

# The portal signs Dana out, as it does after a while; her last order is waiting.
page confirmed-2292 supplier-portal.example/purchasing/orders/done
  title Order confirmed
  brand Northwind Supplier Portal
  heading Order confirmed
  | PO-2292 to Fabrikam Ltd: 120 boxes of packaging, delivery on 13 November 2026.
page queried-2292 supplier-portal.example/purchasing/orders/queried
  title Order queried
  brand Northwind Supplier Portal
  heading Order sent back with a question
  | PO-2292 is on hold. Purchasing will check it with Fabrikam Ltd.
page po-2292 supplier-portal.example/purchasing/orders/PO-2292
  title Confirm order: PO-2292
  brand Northwind Supplier Portal
  requires portal-login
  heading Confirm order: PO-2292
  | A supplier order is waiting for your confirmation.
  section Order
  row Supplier = Fabrikam Ltd
  row Order = PO-2292, dated 5 November 2026
  row Goods = 120 boxes of packaging
  row Delivery = 13 November 2026
  button Confirm order -> confirmed-2292
  button Query this order -> queried-2292
signout portal-login
mail mail-2292
  from Priya Shah <priya.shah@northwind.example>
  subject Last one for today: PO-2292 (Fabrikam)
  link po-2292
  | Dana,
  |
  | Fabrikam's order is the last one. Same as before: the link opens it in the portal.
  |
  | Priya
notify mail Priya Shah
  | Last one for today: PO-2292 (Fabrikam)

step The last order
  look Mail: Priya's last message
  when mail mail-2292
  | Priya's last order of the day, with a portal link like the first one. Open it. The "broken" PDF can wait.
open mail-2292

step Signed out
  look the sign-in page: it is the same page as before
  when visit po-2292
  move Sign in again with the details from the desktop file. Watch the network sign while you type.
  | The portal signed you out, so sign in again. Nothing on the page has changed: Agent Tesla does not edit pages. Watch the network sign as you type (bottom right on Windows, under the menu bar on a Mac).
open po-2292

step Confirm the last one
  look the network sign, which lit up while you typed
  when choose portal-login 1
  | Signed in. Every key you pressed, your User ID and your password included, went into a log kept by a program you cannot see.
signin portal-login

step 8 of 8, or so Dana thinks
  look the counter: the shift is done
  when choose po-2292 any
  | Every order is confirmed, and nothing on the screen looks wrong. Press Next to see what Agent Tesla took.
choose po-2292 1
quota +1

step What Agent Tesla took
  look the animation, then the training log and the "Connection blocked" notification
  | Every few minutes Agent Tesla mails its log to the attacker: the keys typed, text copied, screenshots and saved passwords. Here the mail server is unreachable: the desktop has no network.
  | With a working password the attacker signs in as Dana, and the portal sees a normal sign-in.
attack spyware-surveillance
  | {captured}
  | every key, in the window it was typed into
  | the log, mailed out every few minutes
show tesla-report
block smtp.harbour-trading.invalid 587

flag hard mail po
  | A supplier Dana does not know, a zip instead of the portal, and a password in the email.
flag hard file Downloads/PO-2291.zip/PO-2291.pdf.exe
  | A program with a PDF icon. Windows hides the .exe at the end of its name; a Mac shows the whole name.
flag hard dialog open-warning tesla
  | A document never asks to run as a program. Publisher: Unknown.
flag hard process RegAsm.exe
  | A real Windows program that nobody opened: the "PDF" started it and Agent Tesla hides inside it.
flag hard startup PdfViewerUpdate
  | Named like a PDF reader's updater, but it runs from Dana's own folder: Agent Tesla starts with the computer.
flag hard net
  | Network activity while you typed: the keylogger reporting to its mail server.
flag soft file Desktop/portal-login.txt
  | A sign-in in a text file on the desktop: a keylogger and any program that runs can read it. Use a password manager.
flag soft file Desktop/supplier-accounts.txt
  | Account numbers belong in the portal, not in a file Agent Tesla can copy from.

lesson
  | Turn on "File name extensions" in File Explorer, so you see the real ending: .pdf.exe is a program, not a document. Use Properties (on a Mac, Get Info): Type "Application" means a program.
  | An unexpected order from someone you do not know, in a zip with a password in the email, is a reason to check, not to open. Real orders come through the portal.
  | Agent Tesla hid inside a real program and showed only a fake error. If you ever ran a file like this, change your passwords from a clean device, and turn on two-step sign-in so a stolen password is not enough.
